%C - This is a VPU Encoder unit-test for file-to-file mode

Syntax:
    vpu_encoder_test <options>

Options (describes primary options, run with -h for more details)
    h               Help
    cfgFileName     Encoder Config parameters (mandatory)
    codec           Codec format (mandatory if using non HEVC encoded input files). Use 0 for AVC, and 12 for HEVC
    enable-uvintlv  Enables Interleaved UV (CbCr) support, for NV12 input frames
    input           Input YUV file to encode (optional). Overrides 'InputFile' in cfg file if defined
    output          Output encoded file (mandatory to store encoded binary into a file)
    coreIdx         Codec instance to use (default: 0), instance 1 is supported only on J784S4 SoCs.

Examples:
    # Basic help built into the executable
    vpu_encoder_test -h

    # AVC file-to-file encode
    vpu_encoder_test --codec 0 --enable-uvintlv --cfgFileName /ti_fs/codec_test/vpu/cfg/avc_inter_8b_02.cfg --output /ti_fs/codec_test/vpu/output/avc_inter_8b_02.cfg.264 --coreIdx 0

    # HEVC file-to-file encode
    vpu_encoder_test --enable-uvintlv --cfgFileName /ti_fs/codec_test/vpu/cfg/hevc_bg_8b_01.cfg --output /ti_fs/codec_test/vpu/output/bg_8b_01.cfg.265 --coreIdx 0

Notes:
    - This test is applicable only on J721S2  & J784S4 SoCs
